NAME
    trial - execute, judge, and record a test selection

SYNOPSIS
    trial [--tier T] [--from FILE] [--no-reuse] [--dry-run]
          [--on RUNNER] [--requested-by WHO] [--base REV] [--repo DIR]
    trial verdict SHA
    trial ls
    trial show N
    trial quarantine [add TEST --owner O --cause C [--unit U]
                      [--days N] | rm TEST]

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.testing module. Reads an impact(1) selection
    from standard input or --from FILE (or computes one automatically
    against --base for --tier), executes the selected units, renders a
    GREEN or RED verdict, and records the trial in the store.

    Execution stages:
    - Cargo roots run once each with selected crates passed via '-p'
      under cargo-nextest (using the tier profile such as 'test-fast'
      when defined, else release), with JUnit reporting and retries
      (1 retry normally, 2 for quarantined tests).
    - .NET test projects run dotnet build followed by dotnet test
      --no-build with the selected filter and TRX logging, retrying
      failed tests once by name to detect flakes.
    - The 'lunap' unit runs dotnet test in the sibling LunaP checkout.

    Steps execute concurrently inside queue(1) CPU slots under a
    resource-capped systemd scope (CPUWeight=20, MemoryMax=10G or
    EMUSEN_TESTING_MEMORY_MAX, MemorySwapMax=2G). Trials run past the
    shell's 10-second loop budget and forward Ctrl-C to child steps.

    On tiers enabling reuse (fast, land), a unit whose units(1) key
    matches a recent green run on the same runner with no flakes in 30
    days is skipped and reported as 'reused'. Units with uncommitted
    inputs have no key and always run; nightly never reuses.

    A failing test fails its unit. A flaky test also fails its unit
    unless actively quarantined by name (max 14-day expiry; renewal
    requires a new cause). Subcommands query stored trials and manage
    quarantines: 'verdict SHA' prints the latest verdict for a tree,
    'ls' lists the last 20 trials, 'show N' displays trial N, and
    'quarantine' lists, adds, or removes quarantine entries.

OPTIONS
    --tier T            Tier name (default: land).
    --from FILE         Read selection lines from FILE.
    --no-reuse          Disable cached green-result reuse.
    --dry-run           Plan and print steps without running tests.
    --on RUNNER         Runner name (currently only 'desktop').
    --requested-by WHO  Caller tag recorded on the trial.
    --base REV          Base revision when computing selection
                        (default: WiseMan).
    --repo DIR          Git repository root (overrides EMUSEN_REPO).
    --owner O           (quarantine add) Owner responsible for the fix.
    --cause C           (quarantine add) Root-cause description.
    --unit U            (quarantine add) Unit owning TEST.
    --days N            (quarantine add) Expiry in days (default: 14,
                        max: 14).

ENVIRONMENT
    EMUSEN_TESTING_MEMORY_MAX
        Override per-step MemoryMax limit (default: 10G).

EXAMPLES
    impact | trial --dry-run
    impact --base HEAD~1 --head HEAD | trial --requested-by land
    trial --from selection.txt --no-reuse
    trial verdict $(git rev-parse HEAD)
    trial quarantine add 'tests::racy_timer' --unit cargo:Platform/crystal --owner dev --cause "2 ms timing window"

EXIT STATUS
    0   Trial verdict GREEN, verdict subcommand found GREEN, or query/
        quarantine subcommand succeeded.
    1   Trial verdict RED, or verdict subcommand found RED.
    2   Execution error, unsupported runner, invalid options, or verdict
        subcommand found no record for SHA.

SEE ALSO
    impact(1), units(1), results(1), queue(1), ingest(1), shard(1)
